cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both the software and the associated manuscript."
title: "Analysis code for: Thyroid function and atherosclerotic vascular disease — two-sample Mendelian randomization estimates depend on the outcome genome-wide association study used"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23239484"          # concept DOI (all versions); the v1.1.0 version DOI is minted by Zenodo on release
url: "https://github.com/ximeng007cmx/pad_thyroid_mr"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ximeng007cmx/pad_thyroid_mr"
abstract: >-
  Two-sample Mendelian randomization analysis pipeline for three thyroid function
  traits (hypothyroidism, TSH, free T4) against eight atherosclerotic vascular
  outcomes, including a paired design across independently sourced outcome GWAS,
  independent replication, MVMR, reverse MR, colocalization, power analysis and
  the reverse application of the sample-overlap framework of Burgess et al. (2016).
keywords:
  - Mendelian randomization
  - thyroid function
  - hypothyroidism
  - peripheral artery disease
  - atherosclerotic vascular disease
  - sample overlap
  - between-GWAS heterogeneity
  - genetic epidemiology
